    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="1005" n="991" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg991"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">103.9169/2372k: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-03">February 3,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>858. Reference your 327 of January 13 and Department’s 381 of January 15.<anchor
                        n="28" xml:id="d559-f1"/> In view of the fact that the reception of children
                    in Switzerland is to be discussed at the forthcoming economic negotiations,
                    Department and FEA believe that our Mission in Bern should be instructed to
                    associate itself at the first suitable opportunity with the British
                    representations, which we assume from your reference telegram have already been
                    made. We would appreciate your discussing the current British position in the
                    matter with MEW and informing our Legation in Bern of the background of the
                    problem and of the action which we desire should be taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
